  The <strong>stochastic training trick</strong>: during training, the loop count S is drawn uniformly from &#123;1, …, S_max&#125; at each step. This forces the shared mid-block to produce useful representations at any loop depth, making the model deployable with any S at inference — including values beyond S_max = 12 (which still helps, showing the operator generalizes).
</p>

