<!-- §06 -->
<section id="s-results" data-code="results">
<div class="section-no">06 — Results</div>
<h2>3.3× FLOPs saved, +8.5% on math reasoning</h2>
<p>
  All experiments use a 170M-parameter diffusion transformer (rotary PE, adaptive LayerNorm), matched in parameter count and total training FLOPs against a non-looped MDM baseline. The loop is applied to mid-layers 1–2 with S_max = 12. Results are averaged over five random seeds.
</p>

<h3>Training compute efficiency</h3>
<p>
  The headline result: on FineWeb-Edu, LoopMDM reaches the same test NLL as the MDM baseline using <strong>3.34× fewer training FLOPs</strong>. On OpenWebText: 2.95×. On LM1B: 2.34×. When trained at matched total FLOPs, LoopMDM consistently outperforms.
</p>

