<!-- Listen-friendly hidden summary -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display:none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: LoopMDM — Looped Masked Diffusion Language Models</h2>
    <p>Masked Diffusion Language Models generate text by progressively unmasking tokens over many denoising steps. At each step, the transformer predicts all masked positions simultaneously — but cannot revise predictions within a single step, limiting performance on globally-constrained tasks.</p>
    <p>LoopMDM solves this by sharing a small block of early-middle transformer layers and applying it S times per denoising step. This gives the model an effective depth far greater than its parameter count, and lets masked positions iteratively refine each other's predictions. On a Sudoku puzzle with left-to-right generation order, errors drop from 24 at S=1, to 7 at S=2, to 0 at S=3. On language benchmarks, LoopMDM matches baseline quality with 3.3x fewer training FLOPs and improves GSM8K math accuracy by 8.5 points. An adaptive strategy that monitors hidden-state convergence reduces the average loop count from 12 to 5.1 with minimal accuracy loss.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：LoopMDM——循环掩码扩散语言模型</h2>
    <p>掩码扩散语言模型通过在多个去噪步骤中逐步揭示掩码标记来生成文本。在每一步中，Transformer会同时预测所有掩码位置——但无法在单步内修正预测结果，这限制了模型在全局约束任务中的表现。</p>
    <p>LoopMDM通过共享一小组早中期Transformer层并在每个去噪步骤中循环应用S次来解决这一问题。这使模型的有效深度远超其参数量，并允许掩码位置迭代地相互修正预测。在强制从左到右生成顺序的数独谜题上，错误数从S=1时的24个，降至S=2时的7个，再到S=3时的0个。在语言基准测试上，LoopMDM以少3.3倍的训练算力达到基线质量，并将GSM8K数学准确率提升8.5个百分点。一种监控隐藏状态收敛的自适应策略可将平均循环次数从12次减少至5.1次，而性能损失极小。</p>
  </div>
</div>

